---
import Layout from '../layouts/BlogPost.astro';
---

<Layout
	title="About"
	description="Who writes these notes, and what this blog is for."
	pubDate={new Date('2022-07-08')}
>
	<p>
		I'm Putu Chandra, a Shopify developer. This blog collects what I learn while building
		and fixing real stores: the settings that matter, the code that survives contact with
		production, and the tools worth keeping.
	</p>

	<p>
		Every note here is written to be used the same day. No 4,000-word roundups, no
		launch sequences, no newsletters that exist to sell you something. If a post
		doesn't help you ship, it doesn't belong here.
	</p>

	<h2>What this blog covers</h2>

	<ul>
		<li><strong>Store setup:</strong> theme structure, navigation, and the defaults worth changing first.</li>
		<li><strong>Conversion:</strong> product pages, pricing presentation, and checkout friction you can remove.</li>
		<li><strong>Apps and automation:</strong> a small stack that replaces manual work for a solo operator.</li>
	</ul>

	<h2>How to reach me</h2>

	<p>
		The best way to keep up is the <a href="/blog/">blog index</a> or the{' '}
		<a href="/rss.xml">RSS feed</a>. If you found something here useful, that's
		enough. If something is wrong, I'd rather know than not.
	</p>
</Layout>
